* TuxSpice model cards for common diodes that LTspice's standard.dio lacks.
* Written for TuxSpice from datasheet typical values: forward curves are two-point fits
* (IS, N, RS through a low- and a high-current Vf), zeners put IBV = Izt at BV = Vz with
* NBV giving the datasheet Zzt, recovery time -> TT. Approximations, not manufacturer
* models. Iave, Vpk, mfg and type are picker metadata, as in standard.dio.
* tests/test_models.py checks Vf and Vz of each in ngspice.
* rectifiers
.model 1N4001 D(IS=2.8n N=1.74 RS=43m CJO=15p M=0.33 TT=5u BV=50 IBV=5u Iave=1 Vpk=50 mfg=Generic type=silicon)
.model 1N4002 D(IS=2.8n N=1.74 RS=43m CJO=15p M=0.33 TT=5u BV=100 IBV=5u Iave=1 Vpk=100 mfg=Generic type=silicon)
.model 1N4004 D(IS=2.8n N=1.74 RS=43m CJO=15p M=0.33 TT=5u BV=400 IBV=5u Iave=1 Vpk=400 mfg=Generic type=silicon)
.model 1N5408 D(IS=8n N=1.74 RS=15m CJO=40p M=0.33 TT=5u BV=1000 IBV=5u Iave=3 Vpk=1000 mfg=Generic type=silicon)
.model FR107 D(IS=6.7n N=1.9 RS=0.176 CJO=15p M=0.33 TT=300n BV=1000 IBV=5u Iave=1 Vpk=1000 mfg=Generic type=silicon)
.model UF4007 D(IS=14n N=2 RS=0.366 CJO=10p M=0.33 TT=50n BV=1000 IBV=5u Iave=1 Vpk=1000 mfg=Vishay type=silicon)
.model MUR160 D(IS=8.8n N=1.8 RS=0.1875 CJO=12p M=0.33 TT=35n BV=600 IBV=5u Iave=1 Vpk=600 mfg=OnSemi type=silicon)
